@startuml

title Smart Campus Study Room Booking - Domain Class Diagram

class Student {
    - studentId : String
    + viewAvailability()
    + bookRoom(room : Room, startTime : DateTime, endTime : DateTime) : Booking
    + cancelBooking(booking : Booking)
}

class Room {
    - roomId : String
    - blocked : Boolean
    + isAvailable(startTime : DateTime, endTime : DateTime) : Boolean
    + block()
    + unblock()
}

class Booking {
    - bookingId : String
    - startTime : DateTime
    - endTime : DateTime
    - status : String
    + cancel()
    + conflictsWith(other : Booking) : Boolean
    + hasValidDuration() : Boolean
}

class Administrator {
    - administratorId : String
    + blockRoom(room : Room)
    + unblockRoom(room : Room)
    + reviewUsage()
}

class Confirmation {
    - confirmationId : String
    - action : String
    - createdAt : DateTime
}

Student "1" -- "0..*" Booking : makes >
Room "1" -- "0..*" Booking : reserved through >

Administrator ..> Room : manages >
Administrator ..> Booking : reviews usage >

Booking "1" -- "0..*" Confirmation : produces >

note right of Booking
R1: Start must be in the future.
Duration must be > 0 and <= 2 hours.

R2: Active bookings for the same
room must not overlap.
end note

note right of Room
R3: A blocked room cannot
accept a new booking.
end note

note right of Confirmation
R4 / US-06:
Successful booking produces
a confirmation.
Cancellation also produces
confirmation according to US-06.
end note

note as ASSUMPTIONS
Assumptions:
1. Each Booking belongs to exactly one Student.
2. Each Booking reserves exactly one Room.
3. A Student may have zero or many bookings.
4. A Room may have zero or many bookings over time.
5. Administrator actions are modeled as dependencies,
   not ownership relationships.
6. Confirmation is modeled because R4 and US-06
   explicitly require confirmation.
7. No inheritance or composition is assumed.
8. Payments, equipment, recurring bookings,
   waiting lists and registration are not modeled.
end note

@enduml